mingw defines neither _MSC_VER nor O_NONBLOCK, so FOpen() takes the POSIX
branch and fails to compile:

  time_zone_info.cc:416:40: error: use of undeclared identifier 'O_NONBLOCK'

Fall back to 0 the way the line above already does for O_CLOEXEC. Opening
non-blocking guards against a FIFO or device node, which open() cannot
reach on Windows anyway; the S_ISREG check that follows still applies.

This is the time_zone_info.cc hunk of abseil ddbdebc (Import of CCTZ from
GitHub), due in the next release.

--- a/absl/time/internal/cctz/src/time_zone_info.cc
+++ b/absl/time/internal/cctz/src/time_zone_info.cc
@@ -413,6 +413,9 @@ inline FilePtr FOpen(const char* path) {
 #ifndef O_CLOEXEC
 #define O_CLOEXEC 0
 #endif
+#ifndef O_NONBLOCK
+#define O_NONBLOCK 0
+#endif
   const int fd = open(path, O_RDONLY | O_NONBLOCK | O_CLOEXEC);
   if (fd >= 0) {
     struct stat st;
